n by doing  this there isn't there is more in the  sense that for example um we're  expecting planning reforms to be uh  ditched or  heavily diluted in the queen's speech  next month and there was plans for  radical planning  and that is going to please mps in the  south rather than just red wall mps so i  think it's a bit more  wide-ranging than some of the initial  things which i think were viewed as  almost you know greatest hits for  immediate effect  lastly katie it's been a tough week for  chancellor rishi sumac he has been  falling in several polls and there's  news today  about his wife's tax status tell us  what's been happening and what it means  for the chancellor  so i think we've seen wish you see next  personal approving ratings slowly  dropping um you know in recent months  and in a way that was inevitable he  ended last year as the most popular  politician in the country um he was  spending a lot of money for the first uh  you know  of his time as chancellor and and as  time goes on i think it was always the  case it was going to dip with the spring  statement that's been very sudden you  have a yougov poll this week which  suggests that he is now behind kirstama  and kirsten is also in the negative so  now all politicians in terms of the main  ones are in the negative so it's not  quite something i think to write home  back for the labour leader um but and  there was also a corner home cabinet  leaked table which is by tory members  and richard cena has dropped to the  bottom three boris jones has moved up so  clearly there is the tide is turning to  a degree  what is interesting is as the moon music  around richie's scenic changes and  people are finding more issues with him  i think uh things that in the past  haven't become live political issues  just like labour trying such as such as  risky cena's wealth and now are being  weaponized once again so we saw a story  this week about rishi soon like um  donating um over a hundred thousand  pounds i 